human_hint_en:
Refer to the following dog care precautions to generate a video of the dog in the care chart:
The ingredients of pet wipes are safe and can be used to wipe tear stains, paws, and mouth after returning from taking a bath or walking the dog;
Dogs are generally washed once every two months in spring and summer, and once a month in autumn and winter. Using a bathtub can fully circulate the shower gel all over the body and wash it more cleanly;
Dogs generally have their own "dog smell", and they usually smell when they excrete in their urinal pads. They need to use deodorant regularly to remove the smell and sterilize;
A poop bag is a must-have when walking your dog. Be a quality poop scooper.

